### 8. Wholesale Pricing and Quotation Engine

This is a core business requirement and must be implemented correctly.

#### Tiered pricing

Allow administrators to configure tiers for each product, product variant, or eligible customer price list.

Example demonstration data:

| Quantity | Unit price |
|---|---:|
| 24–49 pairs | $65 |
| 50–99 pairs | $58 |
| 100–249 pairs | $52 |
| 250+ pairs | $48 |

These figures are illustrative only. They must be editable and must never be presented as the business's real prices until confirmed.

The system must support:

- Minimum and maximum quantity boundaries.
- Minimum order quantities.
- Configurable carton multiples.
- Per-product and per-variant pricing.
- Company-specific negotiated prices.
- Quantity-based discounts.
- Configurable currency.
- Effective dates for price changes.
- Quote-specific prices.
- Tax and shipping calculations where configured.
- Price validity periods.
- Clear display of the selected pricing tier.

Define whether tiers apply to individual SKUs, individual variants, or eligible combined quantities. Make the rule explicit in the admin configuration.

Do not automatically combine quantities across different boot models unless the configured pricing policy permits it.

Calculate authoritative prices on the server. Never trust a client-submitted price, discount, subtotal, tax amount, or quote total.

Use decimal-safe monetary calculations and explicit currency handling.

